>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Published compound 4-Br is Cp(CO)₂CrSiBr(IMe₂iPr₂)₂. The silicon in the crystal is four-coordinate. The two input carbene C–Si82 distances are 2.005 and 1.976 Å (WBOs 0.743 and 0.816). Represent both equivalently as neutral NHC donors, C→Si, Use endocyclic N⁺=C⁻ to close the valence shell; Retain Si–Br, Cr–Si and Cp⁻. Localized 5 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 83 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 79 nonmetal covalent bonds: 76 within range, 0 outside range and 3 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

