>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Interactively reviewed graph. Ni–N–O 179.64°, N–O 1.14860 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.9585. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +0 and total charge +1. The authors' CIF identifies the PF₆ salt of the η⁶-anisole nickel nitrosyl. Anisole is neutral and the complex ion carries +1, Near-linear Ni(0)/NO⁺ is a formal representation consistent with the related nickel–arene series. Localized 6 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 19 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 17 nonmetal covalent bonds: 16 within range, 0 outside range and 1 with sparse controls.

