>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1021/ic301176b","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/4330636.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The H14 input retains two terminal imine N atoms without hydrogen, Both interact strongly with Pt. The limiting form uses two neutral terminal imine radicals, one endocyclic N⁻, one Cl⁻ and Pt(II). This open-shell Lewis representation balances the supplied input; The reported species with two N–H bonds is recorded separately. Localized 18 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Spin coupling awaits verification

